    "title": "NCAA Women's Tournament bracket, March Madness first round TV schedule",
    "text": "March 15, 2026Updated March 16, 2026, 8:13 a.m. CTThe 2026 NCAA Women's Tournament bracket was revealed on Sunday.Vanderbilt's chances at a 1-seed took a hit with the one-and-done SEC Tournament run last week. But the Commodores nevertheless will be hosting in the first weekend of the NCAA Tournament.Texas and South Carolina grabbed two 1-seeds for the deep SEC.Keep tabs on this page for brackets, pairings and TV schedules for the 2026 NCAA Women's Tournament. 2026 NCAA Women's Tournament printable bracket2025 NCAA Women's Tournament Printable bracket (PDF) 2026 NCAA Women's Tournament first round scheduleRegion 1 -- Fort WorthIn Storrs, Connecticut (Saturday)1-seed UConn (34-0) vs. 16-seed UTSA (18-15), 2 p.m. on ABC8-seed Iowa State (22-9) vs. 9-seed Syracuse (23-8), 4:30 p.m. on ESPN2In Chapel Hill (Friday)5-seed Maryland (23-8) vs. 12-seed Murray State (31-3), 2 p.m. CT on ESPNU4-seed UNC (26-7) vs. 13-seed Western Illinois (26-5), 4:30 p.m. CT on ESPNewsIn Columbus (Saturday)6-seed Notre Dame (22-10) vs. 11-seed Fairfield (28-4), 1 p.m. CT on ESPN3-seed Ohio State (26-7) vs. 14-seed Howard (26-7), 10:30 a.m. CT on ESPN2In Nashville (Saturday)7-seed Illinois (21-11) vs. 10-seed Colorado (22-11), 8:30 p.m. CT on ESPN22-seed Vanderbilt (27-4) vs. 15-seed High Point (27-5), 6 p.m. CT on ESPNewsRegion 2 -- SacramentoIn Los Angeles (Saturday)1-seed UCLA (31-1) vs. 16-seed Cal Baptist (23-10), 9 p.m. CT on ESPN8-seed Oklahoma State (23-9) vs. 9-seed Princeton (26-3), 6:30 p.m. CT on ESPN2In Minneapolis (Friday)5-seed Ole Miss (23-11) vs. 12-seed Gonzaga (24-9), 2:30 p.m. on ESPN24-seed Minnesota (22-8) vs. 13-seed Green Bay (25-8), 5 p.m. on ESPNUIn Durham (Friday)6-seed Baylor (24-8) vs. 11-seed Nebraska/Richmond First Four winner, 1 p.m. on ESPN3-seed Duke (24-8) vs. 14-seed Charleston (27-5), 10:30 a.m. on ESPN2In Baton Rouge (Friday)7-seed Texas Tech (25-7) vs. 10-seed Villanova (25-7), 7:30 p.m. on ESPNU2-seed LSU (27-5) vs. 15-seed Jacksonville (24-8), 5 p.m. on ESPNRegion 3 -- Forth WorthIn Austin (Friday)1-seed Texas (31-3) vs. 16-seed Missouri State/Stephen F. Austin First Four winner, 3 p.m. CT on ESPN8-seed Oregon (22-12) vs. 9-seed Virginia Tech (23-9), 12:30 p.m. CT on ESPN2In Morgantown (Saturday)5-seed Kentucky (23-10) vs. 12-seed James Madison (26-8), 1:30 p.m. on ESPNU4-seed West Virginia (27-6) vs. 13-seed Miami (OH) (28-6), 4 p.m. on ESPNUIn Louisville (Saturday)6-seed Alabama (23-10) vs. 11-seed Rhode Island (28-4), 1:30 p.m. on ESPNews3-seed Louisville (27-7) vs. 14-seed Vermont (27-7), 11 a.m. on ESPNIn Ann Arbor (Friday)7-seed NC State (20-10) vs. 10-seed Tennessee (16-13), 7 p.m. CT on ESPN2-seed Michigan (25-6) vs. 15-seed Holy Cross (23-9), 4:30 p.m. CT on ESPN2Region 4 -- SacramentoIn Columbia, S.C. (Saturday)1-seed South Carolina (31-3) vs. 16-seed Southern/Samford First Four winner, 12 p.m. CT on ABC8-seed Clemson (21-11) vs. 9-seed USC (17-13), 2:30 p.m. CT on ESPN2In Norman (Friday)5-seed Michigan State (22-8) vs. 12-seed Colorado State (27-7), 6:30 p.m. CT on ESPNews4-seed Oklahoma (24-7) vs. 13-seed Idaho (29-5), 9 p.m. CT on ESPNIn Fort Worth (Friday)6-seed Washington (21-10) vs. 11-seed South Dakota State (27-6), 1:30 p.m. on ESPNews3-seed TCU (29-5) vs. 14-seed UC San Diego (24-8), 11 a.m. on ESPNIn Iowa City (Saturday)7-seed Georgia (22-9) vs. 10-seed Virginia/Arizona State First Four winner, 12:30 p.m. CT on ESPN22-seed Iowa (26-6) vs. 15-seed Fairleigh Dickinson (30-4), 3 p.m. CT on ESPN What channel is the NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament selection show today?TV channel: ESPNStreaming: ESPN app, FUBO (free trial available)The 2026 NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament selection show will be broadcast nationally on ESPN. Streaming options for the bracket reveal include the ESPN app and FUBO, which offers a free trial to potential subscribers. NCAA Women's Tournament selection show start timeDate: Sunday, March 15Start time: 8 p.m. Eastern/7 p.m. Central NCAA Women's Basketball Tournament sites, datesFirst Four, first and second round gamesMarch 18 and 19: First Four games on campus sitesMarch 20-23: First and second round games on campus sitesSweet 16 and Elite EightMarch 27-30: Fort Worth, TexasMarch 27-30: SacramentoFinal Four and National ChampionshipApril 3 and 5: Phoenix",
